  "title": "S4 colourings of knots are #P-hard; metabelian targets stay polynomial with bounded homology",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups with bounded first homology into finite groups",
  "conclusion": "Counting homomorphisms from knot groups (first homology Z) to S4 that send meridians to transpositions is #P-hard: on tripled alternating diagrams of plane graphs the S3 colourings are free potentials, and the S4 lifts follow the left-right cycles of each monochromatic subgraph, giving a twelve-state model equal to the 12-state Potts model at v = 1/2 for links. Every group with an abelian normal subgroup and nilpotent quotient stays polynomial with bounded mod-p homology.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
